      Verify the subscription ID update:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ az account show"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"{\n  \"environmentName\": AzureStackCloud\",\n  \"id\": \"33212d16-bdf6-45cb-b038-f6565b61edda\",\n  \"isDefault\": true,\n  \"name\": \"Subscription Name\",\n  \"state\": \"Enabled\",\n  \"tenantId\": \"8049c7e9-c3de-762d-a54e-dc3f6be6a7ee\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"name\": \"you@example.com\",\n    \"type\": \"user\"\n  }\n}"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      <li>Record the <code>tenantId</code> and <code>id</code> parameter values from the output. You need these values during the OpenShift Container Platform installation.</li>
      <li>
      Create the service principal for your account:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ az ad sp create-for-rbac --role Contributor --name <service_principal> \\\n  --scopes /subscriptions/<subscription_id> \\\n  --years <years>"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;service_principal&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the service principal name.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;subscription_id&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the subscription ID.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;years&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the number of years. By default, a service principal expires in one year. By using the <code>--years</code> option you can extend the validity of your service principal.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <CodeBlock code={"Creating 'Contributor' role assignment under scope '/subscriptions/<subscription_id>'\nThe output includes credentials that you must protect. Be sure that you do not\ninclude these credentials in your code or check the credentials into your source\ncontrol. For more information, see https://aka.ms/azadsp-cli\n{\n  \"appId\": \"ac461d78-bf4b-4387-ad16-7e32e328aec6\",\n  \"displayName\": <service_principal>\",\n  \"password\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"tenantId\": \"8049c7e9-c3de-762d-a54e-dc3f6be6a7ee\"\n}"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>Record the values of the <code>appId</code> and <code>password</code> parameters from the previous output. You need these values during OpenShift Container Platform installation.</li>
      </ol>
